# Native UI — Guardias

**Goal:** Style with NativeWind (Tailwind `className`); use real platform-native controls. HIG/SwiftUI on iOS, Material via Jetpack Compose on Android — not a cross-platform Material Design 3 / Paper kit.

## Preferred stack

### Styling — NativeWind

- Use **[NativeWind](https://www.nativewind.dev/)** for layout, spacing, typography scale, and colors via `className`.
- Prefer utility classes over large `StyleSheet.create` blocks for app chrome and screens.
- Import CSS-enabled primitives from `src/tw` (re-exports `react-native-css/components`) when using `className`.
- Keep Tailwind theme tokens in CSS (`src/global.css` / `@theme`); avoid one-off hardcoded colors when a token exists.
- For setup/troubleshooting, use the Expo agent skill **`expo-tailwind-setup`** (`.agents/skills/expo-tailwind-setup`).

### Controls — platform native

- Use **[`@expo/ui`](https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v55.0.0/sdk/ui/)** when it fits the platform and SDK.
  - **iOS:** SwiftUI via `@expo/ui/swift-ui` (wrap trees in `Host`). Native stack large titles + SF Symbol header items via React Navigation.
  - **Android:** Jetpack Compose / Material via `@expo/ui/jetpack-compose` (FAB, buttons, etc.). Use the standard native stack Top App Bar (`title`) — do **not** force iOS `headerLargeTitle` on Android.
  - When Compose is unavailable (e.g. Expo Go limitation), fall back to RN primitives with reliable inline styles — never Paper.
- Icons: platform-native (SF Symbols on iOS; Material Symbols / XML drawables on Android Compose). `@expo/vector-icons` only as a temporary RN fallback.

NativeWind and `@expo/ui` complement each other: NativeWind styles layout/chrome; `@expo/ui` / RN primitives provide interactive controls.

## Do not

- Do **not** implement Material Design 3 as a **cross-platform** design system (no MD3 chrome on iOS)
- Do **not** use the `material-3` agent skill for Guardias UI
- Do **not** add new `react-native-paper` components or themes (`PaperProvider`, `MD3LightTheme`, etc.)
- Do **not** invent a custom “Material-like” look to approximate MD3 on iOS

## Migration note

`react-native-paper` may still be in `package.json` until removed. When touching UI, prefer NativeWind + `@expo/ui` / RN primitives rather than extending Paper.
